<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bad Waldsee</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Waldsee</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bad Waldsee is a spa town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-swabia">Upper Swabia</a>, in the Ravensburg district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Its old town lies between two lakes. For centuries the town and its lordship were held by the Truchsesses of Waldburg, who built up a cluster of lands around it, and it passed to Württemberg in 1806. It has been a spa, known for its moor baths, since the mid-20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bad-waldsee.jpg" alt="Bad Waldsee" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ssch · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BadWaldseeStadtsee.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
